User labels (h89s): free-text tags on an item, distinct from the plugin's display **type**. They
ride their own observed-remove OR-set, so re-adding the same label still leaves one, and a remove
only detaches what it observed. Filter the board to a label with `--label`.

Set up a workspace and create an item to label:

```console
$ nxf init --plugin issue-tracker --json
[..]

```

```console
$ nxf create --type bug --title "Fix login" --description "Users cannot log in" --priority P1 --json
[..]

```

Attach two labels (idempotent), then list them — sorted and de-duplicated:

```console
$ nxf label add ab12.0001 urgent --json
{"msg":"ab12.0001 labelled urgent","ok":true}

```

```console
$ nxf label add ab12.0001 backend --json
{"msg":"ab12.0001 labelled backend","ok":true}

```

```console
$ nxf label list ab12.0001 --json
["backend","urgent"]

```

Filter the board to a label (only the labelled item is returned):

```console
$ nxf list --label urgent --json
[..]

```

Detach one label (observed-remove); the other remains:

```console
$ nxf label remove ab12.0001 urgent --json
{"msg":"ab12.0001 unlabelled urgent","ok":true}

```

```console
$ nxf label list ab12.0001 --json
["backend"]

```
